      "id": "sol.amc-8-1986-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Estimating,\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{300^5}{30 \\cdot 400^4} &= 10 \\left(\\dfrac{300}{400}\\right)^4 \\\\ &= 10 \\left(\\dfrac34\\right)^4 \\\\ &= 10 \\cdot \\dfrac{81}{256} \\approx 3. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Round the numbers: \\(304 \\approx 300,\\) \\(29.7 \\approx 30,\\) and \\(399 \\approx 400\\)",
        "Simplify \\(\\dfrac{300^5}{30 \\cdot 400^4} = 10 \\left(\\dfrac34\\right)^4\\)"
      ],
